Drop xkbcommon's X11 FFI

The X11 FFI links the unavailable libxkbcommon-x11; gpui uses only
Wayland, so it is dead code. The x11 feature cannot be turned off: it
comes from gpui_linux's dependency spec, and rules_rs resolves features
from unpatched metadata.

The patch removes a module declaration and a cfg attribute, too little
of the crate to attribute.

diff --git a/src/xkb/mod.rs b/src/xkb/mod.rs
index ddc88e9..815d06e 100644
--- a/src/xkb/mod.rs
+++ b/src/xkb/mod.rs
@@ -9,9 +9,6 @@ pub mod compose;
 pub mod ffi;
 pub mod keysyms;
 
-#[cfg(feature = "x11")]
-pub mod x11;
-
 pub use self::compose::*;
 use crate::xkb::ffi::*;
 
